# Website reference image generation

This specialist generates website design comps. It is not the default frontend coding workflow. Confirm that an image-generation capability actually exists; if unavailable, disclose it rather than pretending that text or code is an image.

## Essential output contract

- **One separate horizontal image per section, generated in its own call.** Never combine sections into one tall board/collage or omit the rest after one image. For sequential-only tools, deliver and label every section in order.
- Preserve the source's scope defaults: hero = 1; landing/site template/product/portfolio = 6; full website/marketing site = 8 when the brief provides no count. Read the detailed count guidance for a multi-section request.
- The user brief overrides aesthetic defaults. Pick audience, narrative/conversion purpose, hero scale and composition intentionally; avoid repeatedly defaulting to text-left/image-right. Maintain one palette/type/CTA/radius/media world across the entire set.
- Images must be readable and implementation-friendly: genuine hierarchy, scale, spacing, controls and media treatment, not abstract mood art. Clear text and contrast, restrained first viewport, varied section rhythm and real visual assets are essential.
- Create a consistent plan before rendering, honor requested counts and brand, inspect output quality, and regenerate unclear sections. Do not switch into application implementation unless the user separately requests that stage.

